                "dc.identifier.page_to" : [ {
                  "value" : "0",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.repealed" : [ {
                  "value" : "false",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.section_id" : [ {
                  "value" : "106073",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.section_number" : [ {
                  "value" : "51",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.section_page_note" : [ {
                  "value" : "<span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span>(1) Every master of a foreign vessel shall, before proceeding to sea from any port or place in India, ensure that the vessel has the requisite number of seafarers of appropriate grades in compliance with the Safety Convention and Standards of Training, Certification and Watchkeeping for Seafarers Convention.<br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 0;\"/> <span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span>(2) A surveyor or any person authorised in this behalf by the Central Government may, at any reasonable time, go onboard a vessel for the purpose of ensuring that the seafarers holding certificates granted in accordance with the Safety Convention and Standards of Training, Certification and Watchkeeping for Seafarers Convention are actually appointed and are present, and satisfy himself about the adequacy of such seafarers for the watchkeeping duties in ports and at sea.<br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 0;\"/> <span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span>(3) If a surveyor or any person authorised under sub-section (<i>2</i>) reports any deficiency in a foreign vessel in relation to the requirements of the Safety Convention and Standards of Training, Certification and Watchkeeping for Seafarers Convention and the Central Government is satisfied that it is unsafe for such vessel to proceed to sea, that vessel may be detained by the proper officer till such requirements are fulfilled.<br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 0;\"/>",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.state_id" : [ {
                  "value" : "1",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.state_name" : [ {
                  "value" : "CENTRAL",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
